course: dictionary
lesson: 15625
title: Teens: the years from 13 to 19
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word teens comes from the numbers that end in «-teen», such as thirteen, fourteen, fifteen and so on up to nineteen. Your teens are the years when your age ends in «-teen».
explain: «She is in her teens.» This means she is aged 13 to 19. «Books for teens» means books written for young people of that age.
explain: In maths, the teen numbers are often learnt together. Watch out: «thirteen» is 13, but «thirty» is 30. Only the teen numbers end in «-teen»; the «-ty» numbers are the tens.
explain: Teens can also talk about temperatures. «It was in the low teens today» means about 13 to 15 degrees. Check the meaning by putting it in the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: Teens are the years of your life when your age ends in «-teen», from 13 to 19.
fact: Teens are also teenagers: young people aged 13 to 19.
fact: «Thirteen» means 13, and «thirty» means 30. Do not mix them up.
fact: The teens can mean the numbers from 13 to 19.
fact: «The low teens» means about 13 to 15 degrees when we talk about temperature.
exercise: «Kai is in his teens.» How old could Kai be? | *15 | 40 | 8 | 25
exercise: Which of these numbers is one of the teens? | *17 | 60 | 40 | 30
exercise: «It was in the low teens this morning.» What temperature could that be? | About 0 degrees | About 50 degrees | About 30 degrees | *About 14 degrees
test: «Books for teens» are written for whom? | *Young people aged 13 to 19 | Babies | Adults over 60 | Only grown-up doctors
test: Which word is a teen number? | ninety | twenty | ten | *sixteen
exam: Which sentence uses teens correctly? | *Ella is in her teens, and she is 16 | Her teens are forty years old | The teens is a kind of dog | Teens means the number 30
